WEBVTT

NOTE sequence=threejs-hub-90s aspect=landscape_16x9

c01
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.300 line:82% position:50% align:center
Got spare AI tokens? Eranos puts
them to work for nonprofits.

c02
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.867 line:82% position:50% align:center
A nonprofit types what it needs,
and gets back cited research.

c03
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.833 line:82% position:50% align:center
Work on their own files becomes a
free kit their own agent runs.

c04
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.900 line:82% position:50% align:center
The builder can never approve
its own kit.

c05
00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:29.033 line:82% position:50% align:center
Now that you've seen how AI
serves the public good,

c06
00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:33.900 line:82% position:50% align:center
let's zoom into the Tasks and
Task Objects engine underneath.

c07
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.333 line:82% position:50% align:center
AI is smart. The way we use it
is frustratingly dumb.

c08
00:00:40.733 --> 00:00:44.167 line:82% position:50% align:center
Everything is nouns and verbs,
in plain words.

c09
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:50.700 line:82% position:50% align:center
Muse Code and nanoMuse claim a lease,
and stale leases get refused.

c10
00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:57.833 line:82% position:50% align:center
Herma injects nouns into Meta Muse
Spark, or answers with zero tokens.

c11
00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:02.567 line:82% position:50% align:center
A person makes every decision
about a person.

c12
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:09.500 line:82% position:50% align:center
Seed packs and feeds connect Harness
Square, OpenCode, Pi, and Muse Code.

c13
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:17.067 line:82% position:50% align:center
On synthetic tests, Meta Glimmer 30B
and Llama 3.2 LoRAs store skills.

c14
00:01:18.867 --> 00:01:24.433 line:82% position:50% align:center
This video was made the same way,
with twelve SHA-256 receipts.

c15
00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:27.300 line:82% position:50% align:center
Point your agent at Eranos today.
